  <data name="Nav_Lounge.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Rooms</value></data>
  <data name="Lounge_Heading.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Rooms</value></data>
  <data name="Lounge_Summary.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Pick a host (the server of whoever hosts Beamcast), see its public rooms, jump into a favorite, use a code or invite, or create your own room. Inside, anyone can broadcast their screen and everyone picks what to watch.</value></data>
  <data name="Lounge_Server.Header" xml:space="preserve"><value>Server (host or IP)</value></data>
  <data name="Lounge_Server.PlaceholderText" xml:space="preserve"><value>192.168.1.20 or wss://beamcast.example.com</value></data>
  <data name="Lounge_YourName.Header" xml:space="preserve"><value>Your name</value></data>
  <data name="Lounge_CreateHeading.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Create a lounge</value></data>
  <data name="Lounge_CreateHint.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>The password is required: it becomes the key that encrypts everything end to end. The server never receives it.</value></data>
  <data name="Lounge_Name.Header" xml:space="preserve"><value>Room name</value></data>
  <data name="Lounge_Name.PlaceholderText" xml:space="preserve"><value>e.g. Friends' room</value></data>
  <data name="Lounge_CreatePassword.Header" xml:space="preserve"><value>Password (min. 4 characters)</value></data>
  <data name="Lounge_CreateButton.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Create room</value></data>
  <data name="Lounge_JoinHeading.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Join with a code or invite</value></data>
  <data name="Lounge_JoinHint.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Paste the room code or the BC-… invite you were given. Private rooms can only be joined this way. Invites may carry the key and skip the password.</value></data>
  <data name="Lounge_Code.Header" xml:space="preserve"><value>Code or invite</value></data>
  <data name="Lounge_Code.PlaceholderText" xml:space="preserve"><value>ABC234 or BC-…</value></data>
  <data name="Lounge_JoinPassword.Header" xml:space="preserve"><value>Password (if any)</value></data>
  <data name="Lounge_JoinButton.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Join</value></data>
  <data name="Lounge_SecurityNote.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Names, titles, video and audio are end-to-end encrypted (AES-256-GCM). Password rooms derive the key from the password; without one, a member inside hands the key to the newcomer (ECDH). The host only sees ciphertext, password proofs and invites; it cannot watch or listen.</value></data>
